{"id":"DRKS00033264","src":"drks","title":"A non-interventional study of melphalan flufenamide (melflufen, Pepaxti) in combination with dexamethasone in patients with relapsed and/or refractory multiple myeloma (RRMM) according to the approved label.","official":"","summary":"This study sets out to observe the effectiveness of melflufen in combination with dexamethasone in real life, for example how many patients treated with this combination respond to the therapy, how long time the treatment may hold the disease back and prolong survival. In addition, data will be collected on side effects and other adverse events patients may experience. The influence of the treatment on the patients' quality of life will also be investigated.","conditions":["relapsed and/or refractory multiple myeloma","Multiple myeloma"],"interventions":[{"type":"ARM","name":"Pepaxti  (Melflufen) + Dexamethasone according to marketing authorization administered as part of routine clinical practice"}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\n1. The patient fulfils basic eligibility criteria as described in the observational plan\r\n2. Be at least 18 years of age.\r\n3. Ability to provide signed and dated informed consent.\r\n4. Decision for treatment with the combination therapy melflufen and dexamethasone is made before inclusion in the study.\nExclusion criteria:\n1. Patients who are currently participating in any interventional clinical study (unless the patient only remains in survival follow-up).\r\n2. Any assessment of effectiveness of ongoing melflufen treatment has been performed.\r\n3. Previous treatment with melflufen, or ongoing treatment with melflufen has been longer than 28 days.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":null,"start":"2024-07-16","pcd":"2027-12-31","upd":"2026-11-03","sponsor":"Oncopeptides AB","areas":["oncology","rare"],"central":["iOMEDICO · + 49 761 152420 · harbour@iomedico.com"],"sites":[{"f":"U